hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"252","Narrated by Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman Al-Muradi, narrated by Shuaib, meaning Ibn Al-Layth, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. They mounted horses, and they brought a man from Banu Hanifa, who was called: Thumama bin Uthal, the master of the people of Al-Yamamah, so they tied him to a pole. From the pillars of the mosque, then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out to it and narrated a long story, and said: Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “ Release Thumama.” So he went to a palm tree near the mosque, took a bath, then entered the mosque and said: I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Then he mentioned the rest of the hadith.”"
"253","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abdul Razzaq told us, Abdullah, and Ubayd Allah, the sons of Omar, told us, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that Thumama al-Hanafi was captured, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would come to him and say: “What do you have, O Thumama?” He says: If you kill, you kill a person who has shed a blood, and if you wish, you wish upon a thankful person, and if you return the money, we will give you of it whatever you wish, and they were the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. They, peace and blessings of God be upon him, love ransom, and they say: What will be done by killing this? One day, when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, treated him to Islam, he unbuckled him and sent him to Abu Talha’s courtyard, where he ordered him to wash, so he did. He prayed two rak'ahs, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Your brother’s Islam has become good.”"
